---
import Figure from "../ProjectFigure.astro";
import Video from "../ProjectVideo.astro";
import { asset } from "../../data/profile";
---
<section class="project-section" id="method" aria-labelledby="method-title">
  <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">An integrated research vision</p><h2 id="method-title">Method</h2><p>Connect what a building senses with how it responds.</p></div>
  <Figure id="immunity-framework" />
  <ol class="method-steps immunity-steps">
    <li><h3>Sense</h3><p>Observe indoor conditions, surfaces, and occupant activity.</p></li>
    <li><h3>Predict</h3><p>Model exposure alongside energy use and thermal comfort.</p></li>
    <li><h3>Respond</h3><p>Inform building control and robotic disinfection.</p></li>
    <li><h3>Adapt</h3><p>Consider changing conditions and the people inside.</p></li>
  </ol>
  <div class="immunity-interaction">
    <Figure id="occupant-interaction" />
    <div><p class="eyebrow">People in the loop</p><h3>Health, energy, and everyday experience</h3><p>The building-immunology vision brings occupant preferences and human interaction into the same picture as environmental sensing.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="project-section" id="response" aria-labelledby="response-title">
  <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Material-aware disinfection</p><h2 id="response-title">Robotic response</h2><p>Recognize the surface before choosing the action.</p></div>
  <div class="immunity-response">
    <Video id="surface-materials" />
    <div><h3>Different surfaces, different decisions</h3><p>Material recognition connects the objects a robot sees with a model of surface transmission.</p><p class="scope-note">Illustrated research workflow from Hu and Li (2022). <a href="https://doi.org/10.1111/mice.12811">Read the material-adaptive disinfection paper ↗</a></p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="immunity-workflow"><Video id="adaptive-disinfection" /></div>
</section>
<section class="project-section" id="communities" aria-labelledby="communities-title">
  <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">The biological context</p><h2 id="communities-title">Microbial communities</h2><p>Sample shared spaces. Observe colonies. Compare communities.</p></div>
  <div class="paired immunity-observations"><Figure id="sampling" /><Figure id="culture-2" /></div>
  <Figure id="abundance" />
  <p class="scope-note">Columns represent samples; rows identify taxa; circle size shows relative abundance. The Building M/T chart and school-sampling images are separate source examples. Community composition alone does not establish infection risk.</p>
  <a class="related-project" href={asset("building-digital-twin/")}><span>Related research</span><strong>Explore building simulation and room-level risk ↗</strong></a>
</section>
